{
  "slug": "memory-toolkit",
  "name": "Memory Toolkit",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Session memory lifecycle for Claude Code. Structured handoffs between sessions, workstreams to switch context without losing it, background watcher (Haiku) that captures decisions and corrections in real time, docs pipeline that routes session findings into .claude/rules/, model recommendations per task, and PreCompact hook to survive context compaction. Works alongside CLAUDE.md and auto-memory — no daemon, no vector DB, no external dependencies. MIT licensed.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **11 skills** and **5 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (11): `docs-reflect` (Collect DOC: notes from session, generalize, and propose repo documentation (.claude/rules/, docs/)), `memory` (Project memory — search, workstreams, notes, decisions), `memory-setup` (Initialize or upgrade project memory for memory-toolkit), `park` (Park an idea or task for the next session — save context, don't lose the thought), `reflect` (Session reflection — analyzes what happened, proposes backlog items, captures insights), `session-continue` (Continue a workstream from where you left off — faster than /session-start, no focus selection), `session-end` (Session completion — handoff, reflect, docs-reflect cascade), `session-insights` (Extract insights from past .jsonl sessions — problems, decisions, friction points), and 3 more\n- **Hooks** (5): `UserPromptSubmit`, `PreCompact`, `PostToolUse`, `SubagentStop`, `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install memory-toolkit@claude-community` from `IlyaGorsky/memory-toolkit`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 11,
    "hook": 5
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "Ilya Gorsky"
  },
